           step("Keyword research", "Weeks 2–4", "Find out what words people actually type into search and what they really want when they type them (this is called search intent). Practise grouping related keywords into topics so that each page on a site targets one clear topic. Good keyword research decides which pages a site should have, so take your time to get it right."),
           step("On-page SEO", "Month 2", "Learn to improve what is on each page: titles, meta descriptions, headings, URLs, images, internal links and the quality of the content itself. Practise by rewriting the title and description of a few real pages so they clearly match what the searcher needs. These changes are fully in your control, which makes on-page work the quickest place to show improvement."),
           step("Technical SEO", "Months 2–3", "Learn the technical side: site speed, mobile-friendliness, sitemaps, robots.txt, canonical tags, structured data and the errors shown in Google Search Console. You do not need to be a developer, but you must understand each issue well enough to explain the fix to one. If a page cannot be crawled or indexed, even the best content will not show up in search."),
